{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>At that time YHWH set apart, etc.</b> This refers back to the earlier matter." "<b>At that time</b> — in the first year of your going out from Egypt. You strayed in the calf, and the Levites did not stray; the Omnipresent set them apart from you. And Scripture placed this passage next to the return of the Benei Ya'akan, to say that in this too the Levites did not stray but stood in their faithfulness." "<b>To bear the Ark.</b> The Levites." "<b>To stand before YHWH to serve Him and to bless in His name.</b> The priests — and that is the lifting of the hands (Arachin 11)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:24.652893038Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}